      "message": "the whole file is loaded into memory, including the header. IIUC, text_offset\u003d0 means you are trying to execute the header\n\ni tried adding some padding and setting the offset, but it wasn\u0027t enough to get it working\n\n```\n--- a/guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py\n+++ b/guest/rialto/append_arm64_header.py\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ def append_arm64_header(original_kernel_file, text_offset, new_filename):\n     header_data \u003d {\n         \"code0\": 0,\n         \"code1\": 0,\n-        \"text_offset\": 0,\n+        \"text_offset\": 0x1000,\n         \"image_size\": len(original_data),\n         \"flags\": 0,\n         \"res2\": 0,\n@@ -75,6 +75,8 @@ def append_arm64_header(original_kernel_file, text_offset, new_filename):\n     # Write the header and original data to the new file\n     with open(new_filename, \"wb\") as f:\n         f.write(header_bytes)\n+        for i in range(0, 0x1000 - 64):\n+          f.write((0).to_bytes(1))\n         f.write(original_data)\n\n if __name__ \u003d\u003d \"__main__\":\n```",
