      "message": "That tricked me too. It is using `read_at_*` (similar to `pread`) with an offset of zero, so the second read will read the header again.\n\nIt is more explicit in the `load_arm64_kernel_from_reader` version, where the header is written separately: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/crosvm/kernel_loader/src/arm64.rs;l\u003d132-135;drc\u003d7d2280f04e0d3321fa35a63a855de325777def6d",
